From: phpv <https://github.com/supanadit/phpv>
Subject: [PATCH] zutil.h: drop TARGET_OS_MAC from the classic-MacOS fdopen guard

Modern Apple SDKs define TARGET_OS_MAC=1 in <TargetConditionals.h> for
every Apple platform, so the classic Mac OS branch fired on macOS and
redefined fdopen() to NULL. The real <stdio.h> declaration then expanded
to `FILE *NULL(...)`, failing the build under Xcode 16:

    _stdio.h:318:7: error: to match this '('
    zutil.h:147:33: note: expanded from macro 'fdopen'

Upstream fixed this in zlib 1.3 by guarding on MACOS alone; this applies
the same change to the 1.2.x line that PHP <= 7.4 is pinned to.

Applies to zlib 1.2.9 .. 1.2.13 (phpv pins 1.2.13 for PHP <= 7.4;
older 1.2.x moved the guard and are left untouched).
---
 zutil.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/zutil.h b/zutil.h
index 5ef1f47..d3de2b4 100644
--- a/zutil.h
+++ b/zutil.h
@@ -137,7 +137,7 @@
 #  endif
 #endif
 
-#if defined(MACOS) || defined(TARGET_OS_MAC)
+#if defined(MACOS)
 #  define OS_CODE  7
 #  ifndef Z_SOLO
 #    if defined(__MWERKS__) && __dest_os != __be_os && __dest_os != __win32_os
-- 
2.47.1

